			<div class="content" id="post-content-2290759">
									

<p>Honestly, that was the singular problem I had when describing the effect.</p>
<p>The only way I can explain it, as I did above, is that it's like looking at something you've written on a piece of paper, from the back side. Everything is flipped.</p>
<p>Like the name of the ship. Sure, it says TITANIC on it, but it's written as if someone wrote it through the inside of the ship. Every piece of paper recovered from the ship is illegible unless you hold it up against a light and read it from the back. Even the goddamned ecosystem that lives in the wreckage is flipped around. It's not just that we've discovered another Titanic, but <em>where</em> we found it and what it looks like.</p>

